{
    "background_story": "Babe was a fashion icon of the 1920s, known for her bold sense of stylization. With her razor-sharp bob and penchant for statement pieces, she turned heads on the catwalks of Paris and New York. Babe's style was a fusion of art deco glamour and modernist chic, inspiring a generation of young women to express themselves through fashion. She was a muse to top designers of the era, who would often create custom pieces just for her. Babe's stylization extended beyond her wardrobe, as she was also a talented makeup artist and hairstylist. She popularized the 'cupids bow' lip shape and 'marcel wave' hairstyle, which became hallmarks of the Roaring Twenties. Babe's influence on fashion and beauty continues to be felt today, as a true pioneer of self-expression and personal style.",
